ResourceUnit/lists/*
ResourceUnit_old

# Local configuration and credentials. .env.example is the versioned template;
# .env itself must never be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Claude Code's own machine-local state.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Installed skills. Derived content: the source and a content hash are recorded
# in skills-lock.json, so this directory is reproducible with
#   npx skills add ch-lam/apex-field-notes -a claude-code
# Not committing it keeps one source of truth: a copy edited here is lost on the
# next install, silently, because the installer rewrites the whole directory.
# That is precisely how the field notes were nearly lost while they lived nested
# inside the vendored Oracle skill, which is why they no longer do.
.claude/skills/

# The vendored APEXlang package under .agents/skills/apex/ is deliberately NOT
# ignored, and the asymmetry is intentional: APEXLang/validate.sh executes
# tools/apexctl.mjs from it. A dependency you run gets pinned and committed; one
# you only read gets installed.
